%% references.bib -- ancestry bibliography for hypercuboid-character-gateways
%%
%% Assembled during the September 2026 finite-field literature, provenance and
%% theorem-ancestry audit (see docs/NOVELTY_AND_PROVENANCE.md).
%%
%% Scope. The manuscript's own bibliography (10 entries, inside
%% manuscript/hypercuboid_character_sums.tex, audited in
%% manuscript/REFERENCE_AUDIT.md) covers the K3 / modularity side of the paper and
%% is not duplicated here except for the four entries the ancestry argument needs
%% by name. What this file adds is the finite-field layer the manuscript's
%% bibliography does not cover: quadratic-character sums, prescribed
%% Legendre-symbol patterns, the Weil/Deligne bounds, hyperplane-arrangement point
%% counts, finite projective geometry, coding and oriented-matroid formulations,
%% and function-field Kummer theory.
%%
%% Provenance. Every entry carrying a DOI was generated from that DOI's own
%% registered metadata (Crossref `/transform/application/x-bibtex`) rather than
%% retyped. The three entries with no DOI -- Hirschfeld1998,
%% MacWilliamsSloane1977, BerndtEvansWilliams1998 -- are monographs with no
%% registered DOI; they were transcribed by hand and each carries a `note` saying
%% so. No DOI was invented for any older work.

